  "sculpt": {
    "_about": "THE BACTRIAN CAMEL (2026-11-05, 2nd pass): heavier and lower than the dromedary -- legs 15% shorter (the rig re-made so: the body lowered, the legs shortened), the cannons a quarter thicker, the barrel broader; two conical, floppy humps, each leaning its own way under a lopsided mop of dark wool, the saddle dip between them where the rider sits; dark wool on the neck, a beard hanging under the throat to the chest, sleeves on the forearms, a mane on the poll, against a paler body; a long head, the split upper lip drooping; thick round pads; the tail hanging to the hock with its tuft SHARP PASS 2 (2026-11-08): the pointed parts -- hnaili, hnailo, naili, nailo (4 in all) -- are the engine's sharp `horn`s (sharp.js), made from the field shapes they replaced by tools/creaturegen/sharp/ (claws.py, teeth.py, spikes.py, antlers.py, bills.py): rooted in the body, tips pointed; RE-RUN those after this species' generator. (2026-11-08, ears2.py) The EARS (ears2.py): small round cupped sheets (sharp.js `fin`); the roots faired.",
